@JordanYates 

>While this is caused by insufficient CONFIG_BT_CTLR_TX_BUFFERS, it should be possible for the controller to iterate over queued packets on a characteristic if it is being unsubscribed from and dequeue them before trying to allocate the write response packet.

If the indications have been already sent to the controller from the host, then there is no way according to spec to flush them, and they *will* go out regardless. However, after the host sends the write response for the unsubscribe, the stack should not allow for any additional indications.
